  "content": {
    "id": "v2-5021a0-p9-practice-slot-4-upper-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A carton measuring 0.6 m long, 40 cm wide and 25 cm high is covered in plastic.\n\nWhat area of plastic is needed to cover 250 cartons? Convert your answer to $\\mathrm{m}^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$245\\,\\mathrm{m}^2$",
      "worked": "Write all lengths in centimetres: $0.6\\,\\mathrm{m}=60\\,\\mathrm{cm}$.\n\nSurface area of one carton:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=(60\\times40)\\times2+(60\\times25)\\times2+(40\\times25)\\times2\\\\A&=4800+3000+2000\\\\A&=9800\\,\\mathrm{cm}^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nArea for 250 cartons:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{250}&=9800\\times250\\\\A_{250}&=2\\,450\\,000\\,\\mathrm{cm}^2\\\\A_{250}&=\\frac{2\\,450\\,000}{100^2}\\,\\mathrm{m}^2\\\\A_{250}&=245\\,\\mathrm{m}^2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 70
  },
